From 9d7f25cf0c23bbc7afb2aff5c1d29b9cdef5b370 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Octo <180629317+OctoAlgo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 09:29:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] pos, tp, time, date and teleport bookmarks through the
 title's own natives; by-ID call hook

Debug channel, with VICTORY_NATIVES on (names from VICTORY_NATIVES_NAMES):
 * pos: the player ped's position, heading (degrees) and the clock, read with the title's natives;
 * tp <x> <y> <z> [<heading>]: the title's own setter (the area streams in, the ped is held
   meanwhile), then the read-back;
 * tpsave <name> / tpgo <name> / tpmarks: bookmarks in VICTORY_DEBUG_BOOKMARKS (default
   bookmarks.txt in the channel's folder), one line `name x y z heading pitch hh:mm` (the
   channel's older format; tpgo also sets the clock);
 * time [<hh> <mm> [<ss>]] and date [<day> <month> <year>] (months 1-12; the title counts from 0);
   without arguments they only read.
Trace: the by-ID call path (+0x3de2331 in +0x3de2250: methods of the script-visible classes) goes
through the same dispatch (21 bytes, checked, logged); VICTORY_NATIVES_LOG_PER=<n> keeps only each
native's first n calls in the full log; VICTORY_NATIVES_WATCHMEM watches memory from the start.

